From 12f2f8f795612d2b6f901b690c87793a54e8da3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 02:30:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] Spike: stop recording copies of active values on the FF16
 rate path

A copy of an active scalar is a tape statement, and a move hands over the
slot. Kernel arguments, canopy-shape arguments, the aux reads in
compute_rates and compute_competition_and_slope, and Node::height() are taken
by reference; temporaries written into Internals and a competition split are
moved. Per rate evaluation at 91 nodes, copies fall from 7,180 to about 1,800.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LFsPxk1yy62LrcCbtZUVeB
---
 inst/include/plant/canopy_shape.h                | 16 +++++++++-------
 inst/include/plant/internals.h                   |  6 ++++++
 .../plant/models/ff16_production_kernel.h        | 12 ++++++------
 inst/include/plant/models/ff16_strategy.h        | 10 +++++-----
 inst/include/plant/node.h                        |  2 +-
 inst/include/plant/species.h                     |  6 +++---
 6 files changed, 30 insertions(+), 22 deletions(-)

